# E2: the eight-seat quad arm c2-packed-tp4-8-best-quad (E1 plus QWEN_FAST_QUAD_DRAFT_BLOCKS=2: one 64-row quad draft per block of four seats, (0,1,2,3) and (4,5,6,7)). Its control is E1 (identical tests).
# FIRST HARDWARE RUN of the second quad: the trace for slots 4-7 and the DRAM headroom for two quads (estimated, not measured) are unproven. Runs only if E1 attached (NEEDS in ORDER.txt): an attach refusal
# for an eight-seat-plus-levers reason would repeat here.
# READ: c2_smoke_check clean under its block rules: judged on concurrent8_steady (a blocks profile smoked without it fails), EXACTLY TWO engaged markers (slots 0,1,2,3 and slots 4,5,6,7), at least one
# [PACKED-SELECT] round naming both groups with users=8, a '[PINDIAG] draft mask pooled slots=[4,5,6,7]' and a '[PINDIAG] draft outputs pooled slots=[4,5,6,7]' line (and the same for 0,1,2,3), no 'pooled refused'
# line, no fallback and no disable line. Texts equal E1's. PAIRED CHECK against E1: per request, the accepted tokens and the verify-round counts must be IDENTICAL, because pairs and quads must draft the same
# tokens; a text match alone cannot show the second quad exact (a wrong draft only lowers acceptance), and E3 audits it. A capture refusal falls back to pairs and logs a fallback, which the smoke counts as a
# failure: record which quad and the headroom figures. Duration (estimate): 120 min. Soft.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/next-5 four-card development window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/next-5 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-5a is what B0 builds from the pushed tp4/next-5 commit; every later job serves that one image. A commit of a
# file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-5a
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8-best-quad
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent4_solo,concurrent4,concurrent4_code_equal,concurrent8_code,concurrent8_code_equal,concurrent8_steady,concurrent5_split,concurrent8_drain
